  "project": "hex-tile",
  "question": "Q-004",
  "provenance": "prospective",
  "question_text": "Do the ridges come back when E-021's plate is printed again, unchanged and untouched?",
  "hypothesis": "E-021's ridges are unevenly spaced and cross the whole face, so whole layers were disturbed at a few moments; the model, settings and per-pair toolpath are identical to E-020, which printed clean. So they came from events during that run (the door or lid opened, a filament feed hiccup), not from the model or from sharing the plate.",
  "prediction": "Printed again with the door and lid left shut for the whole print, both strips' fronts are clean. If ridges return, they sit at the same heights as E-021's (the printer's Z) or at new heights (plate sharing or the filament).",
  "why_this_test": "A same-plate repeat is the only test that keeps everything but the run itself the same. A single strip alone would change the plate and the run at once, so it couldn't tell them apart. It also gives a second read on whether the kiss tacks snap apart.",
